  "numbered_assertions_completed": 0,
  "main_theorem_verified": false,
  "scope": "Complete compatible-circuit existence on at most four labels from only the original global half-cut inequalities and even selected degrees. No bounded multiplicity, bounded degree, connectedness, pre-existing partition or selector is assumed. Tight nonlocal shores are normalized, inside and outside partitions are constructed from the proved three-label theorem, and every original copy is restored through disjoint blocks and saved closed pieces. Strict nonlocal inputs have a constructed safely removable pair or triangle; induction uses arbitrary admissible even residuals. Arbitrary selected copy sets and finite label types of size at most four are covered. Original-host applications construct unrestricted even-fiber and two-odd-fiber joining decompositions with exact footprints, including the even-regular half-joining-degree interface. The full four-core terminal Proposition 4.16, Theorem 4.17 and main theorem are not asserted. All 69 numbered records and the 49 completed count remain unchanged.",
